0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6.2.stable, 4.7.beta1\n- Not reproducible in: 4.5.2.stable and older\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable - CachyOS Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT Thu, 23 Apr 2026 21:04:50 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (nvidia; 595.58.03) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-9300H CPU @ 2.40GHz (8 threads) - 15.53 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe Window node position get force changed whenever changing scene or zooming in on it.\n\nIt shouldn't override the position that the user as put in.\n\nI have tried multiple godot version to pinpoint the issue, it doesn't happen in godot 4.5.2.stable and older but it does in 4.6.2, and it happen when changing scene or when zooming, and since with this version when zooming godot redraw the node to update the quality and that feature wasn't in 4.5.2.stable i do believe that's the cause issue.\n\nStrangely enough, the issue is way more apparent when the main window height is higher, as the Window node position snap back after the threshold of the base project height, for example, put the window in the bottom left of the project's base height of 648 and it might not have issue, do it with the set to 1080 and it will happen.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3ed0c630-74db-4b17-b5df-0f4b509ebfd8\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new scene, starting node don't matter\n- Add a Window node to it\n- Move the Window position to the bottom left and then change scene and come back, nothing should happen.\n- Move it a bit lower and change scene again and then come back, position will be set higher.\n- Try changing the size and doing the same thing and it will happen earlier than the main window height\n\nAnd for an even more obvious setup:\n- Create a new scene, starting node don't matter\n- Add a Window node to it\n- change scene and come back, the Window node get moved lower, so it even happen with the default settings.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119180/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119180/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}